    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d352">

                <pb facs="0551" n="481" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg481"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Plumb</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 24.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-11-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 23, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatches Nos. 17 and 1S, of October
                    17th and 18th, respectively, have been received.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * *</p>
                <pb facs="0552" n="482" xml:id="pg482"/>
                <p>Upon a review of the whole matter, your refusal to place your indorsement upon
                    the paper presented to you by A. G. Farine, of the chancellerie of the French
                    legation, meets the approbation of this department.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward L Plumb,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
